idence":["Approach: '~/.local/share and ~/.rebar-serena-mirror are already in ... readwritePaths'","Scope doc bullet: 'the ~/.rebar-serena-mirror prerequisite'","Absence: no statement of what that directory is, how it is created, or the default behavior if it is missing"],"finding":"The entry passes `--project ${HOME}/.rebar-serena-mirror`, and the plan lists it as a documented 'prerequisite', but no scope item or criterion states how `~/.rebar-serena-mirror` comes to exist. If a developer's checkout lacks it, serena may fail to start after this change, yet nothing in the plan defines the expected default or creation step.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3ab10fc581a8d8f5","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Approach — `~/.rebar-serena-mirror` prerequisite","norm_id":"n3d862ec8d210089d","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A second developer runs the headless copilot check on a machine where ~/.rebar-serena-mirror was never created; serena's --project target is missing."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a doc line describing the mirror directory's purpose and its creation command (e.g. the git clone/mirror step) alongside the `uv tool install` prerequisite.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: better","verify command `grep` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the committed `${HOME}/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena` path behaves on Windows (different uv data dir + `.exe`), or scope the entry/docs to POSIX hosts and document the Windows path explicitly.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: command `${HOME}/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena`, args `... --project ${HOME}/.rebar-serena-mirror`","Plan: '`uv tool install ...` produces `~/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena` (confirmed on this host)' — the layout is asserted for one host only","The `.mcp.json` change is committed to a tracked file shared by all developers, so the path ships to every platform in the matrix"],"finding":"The committed, shared `.mcp.json` hardcodes the POSIX/uv-specific absolute path `${HOME}/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena`, confirmed only 'on this host'. On a Windows developer workstation `uv tool install` places tool binaries under a different data directory (e.g. `%LOCALAPPDATA%` / uv's Windows data dir) and produces `serena.exe`, not `.../bin/serena`, so the expanded command path does not exist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd7cb9983794e0c6b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — `.mcp.json` entry command `${HOME}/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena`","norm_id":"n5d565eff3c444d8a","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows developer workstation: a teammate who ran `uv tool install` gets the tool under uv's Windows data dir as `serena.exe`; Copilot expands `${HOME}/.local/share/uv/tools/serena-agent/bin/serena`, the file is absent, and serena fails to launch (file-not-found / broken pipe) — the same class of failure this ticket set out to fix, now on Windows"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify the serena args against the installed binary's own help output — record that `serena start-mcp-server --help` (serena-agent 1.7.1.dev0) lists `--context` and `--project` — and classify the CLI-surface evidence (Verified vs the currently Partially-verified probe of a scratch script).","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Approach quotes probe log `LAUNCHED cmd=/Users/joeoakhart/scratch/mcp-probe/bin/probe.sh args=start-mcp-server --context ide-assistant --project ...` — a scratch probe.sh, not the serena binary, so it confirms Copilot arg-passing but not serena's flag surface","Scope: args `start-mcp-server --context ide-assistant --project ${HOME}/.rebar-serena-mirror`","T3 flag-level empiricism: OBSERVE flag names from --help, do not infer from a prior version — the args are carried over from the old `uvx ... serena start-mcp-server` invocation","serena is external upstream (not importable in this environment: resolve_symbol UNRESOLVED), so the CLI surface is unverifiable from the repo alone"],"finding":"The serena CLI subcommand/flag surface the fix depends on (`start-mcp-server --context ide-assistant --project <path>`) is asserted but not verified against serena-agent's own `--help`. The empirical probe the plan quotes exercised a scratch `probe.sh`, which verifies Copilot's ${HOME}/arg passing — NOT that the installed serena-agent 1.7.1.dev0 binary actually accepts `start-mcp-server`, `--context ide-assistant`, and `--project`. A flag rename between the old uvx build and the pinned prebuilt binary would fail only at the headless-run acceptance stage, not as a named precondition.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc7d89562b44508e6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — serena args `start-mcp-server --co